1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:02,240
So Claude can now read my Twitter feed.

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:03,760
Now I don't like scrolling through X,

3
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:05,200
there are some weird people on X.

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,720
But there's actually a ridiculous amount

5
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:08,440
of very useful information

6
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:09,760
that sometimes gets posted.

7
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:11,740
So I found an open source Python framework

8
00:00:11,740 --> 00:00:12,840
called Browser Use.

9
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:14,960
It allows AI to control your web browser

10
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:15,800
kind of like a human would.

11
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:17,440
And for the local browser version,

12
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:19,040
you don't actually need an X API

13
00:00:19,040 --> 00:00:20,820
or the Browser Use cloud API.

14
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,070
So what I told it to do was go

15
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:23,550
through my X home feed, scroll

16
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:25,140
through roughly like a hundred posts,

17
00:00:25,140 --> 00:00:26,780
ignore the memes, engagement bait,

18
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:29,090
and repeated stories, then find 10 things

19
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:31,040
most relevant to AI agents, developer

20
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:32,800
tools, startups, and new products.

21
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,560
For each, tell me what happened,

22
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:35,960
why it matters, and give me

23
00:00:35,960 --> 00:00:36,800
the original post.

